00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:45,980
You did. You always do. The Proof: Fifty Years of Going Nowhere.

192
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:52,960
Medical Research as percent of G.D.P. In nineteen seventy-five it was zero point zero eight percent.

193
00:21:53,660 --> 00:22:00,280
By nineteen eighty-five, zero point zero seven percent. In nineteen ninety-five, still zero point zero seven percent.

194
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:06,460
In two thousand and five, zero point zero six percent. In twenty fifteen, zero point zero six percent.

195
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:14,620
In twenty twenty-five, zero point zero six five percent. Absolute dollars increased ten times.

196
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:20,530
Share of actual resources: decreased. You got richer and spent less of it on not dying.

197
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:23,800
Like buying a bigger house and removing the smoke detectors.

198
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:29,040
What Actually Grew. The financial sector grew from three percent to eight percent of G.D.P.

199
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:34,680
The military-industrial sector grew from three percent to three point four percent of G.D.P.

200
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:39,160
in direct spending, with broader defense-adjacent industries adding more.

201
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:46,910
Healthcare spending ballooned from seven percent to eighteen percent of G.D.P., but most of that growth is bureaucracy,

202
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:56,140
not cures. The part that actually keeps you alive, the actual medical research, is a shrinking slice of a growing pie.

203
00:22:56,760 --> 00:23:01,240
You baked a bigger pie and gave the science department a smaller plate.

204
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:05,540
The money printers fund what they value. They value control, not cures.

205
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:12,140
Nobody ever seized power with a stethoscope. (Though, medically speaking, you could.).

206
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:18,600
"Just Tax the Billionaires" "Fine," says the progressive who just read the last three subsections.

207
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:23,580
"The problem is inequality. Tax the billionaires. Fund medical research.

208
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:30,720
Simple." Your species has been trying this for a century. Here is the loop: Step one.

209
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:36,080
Progressives raise taxes on the wealthy. Victory. Step two.

210
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:43,540
The wealthy spend a fraction of those taxes on lobbyists who return eighteen dollars for every one dollar invested.

211
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:52,960
They secure one hundred and eighty-one billion dollars per year in direct corporate welfare, fifty billion dollars in fossil

212
00:23:52,960 --> 00:24:01,240
fuel subsidies, and seventy-five billion dollars in agricultural subsidies where the top ten percent of farms collect sixty-three

213
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:10,020
percent of payments. Over three hundred billion dollars per year flows back to the people you just taxed, through programs

214
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:14,420
too boring for voters to monitor and too lucrative for lobbyists to ignore.

215
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:19,840
Step three. The Federal Reserve prints money. Asset prices inflate.

216
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:24,620
In twenty twenty, the Fed created roughly four trillion dollars.

217
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:28,640
The top one percent gained four point two trillion dollars in net worth.

218
00:24:29,340 --> 00:24:34,620
The bottom fifty percent gained eight hundred and thirty billion dollars total.

219
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:40,520
Per person: one point three million dollars versus five thousand dollars.

220
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:47,160
A two hundred and fifty-to-one ratio. The billionaires did not just recover what you taxed.

221
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:55,160
They made more in asset inflation than they lost in taxes, and the inflation bill went to the same working families progressives

222
00:24:55,160 --> 00:25:03,340
were trying to help. Step four. Progressives look at the widening wealth gap and propose: higher taxes on the wealthy.

223
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:13,300
Return to Step one. Repeat for one hundred years. The entire planet spends four point five billion dollars per year testing

224
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:20,520
whether drugs work in humans. One country spends over three hundred billion dollars per year on corporate handouts to people

225
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:28,140
who already have money. The ratio is roughly sixty-eight-to-one for subsidizing wealth over testing cures.

226
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:37,480
Every "tax the billionaires" campaign in history has left this ratio untouched, because the same political system that collects

227
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:46,080
the taxes allocates the spending, and that system has a documented zero percent correlation with what voters actually want.

228
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:53,480
The progressive strategy fails not because the diagnosis is wrong (the allocation is obscene) but because it prescribes

229
00:25:53,480 --> 00:26:00,000
the same treatment that has failed for a century: route more money through a captured system and hope it comes out different

230
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:07,140
this time. The money goes in as taxes. It comes out as subsidies, asset inflation, and an N.I.H.

231
00:26:07,140 --> 00:26:14,100
that spends three point three percent on clinical trials. The pipe leaks faster than you can fill it, and the leaks flow

232
00:26:14,100 --> 00:26:20,000
upward. This is why the one percent treaty doesn't route funding through your existing institutions.

233
00:26:20,340 --> 00:26:23,790
It builds a new pipeline that the lobbyists haven't colonized yet.

234
00:26:23,980 --> 00:26:28,320
You don't fix a rigged game by playing harder. You build a different game.

235
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:37,740
Why Money Printing Matters: Resources Follow the Printer. When the Fed prints one trillion dollars for war, defense contractors

236
00:26:37,740 --> 00:26:42,560
get it first and immediately buy up the best engineers, scientists, and factories.

237
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:49,280
An M.I.T. graduate with two hundred thousand dollars in student debt chooses between Raytheon at one hundred and fifty thousand

238
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:53,180
dollars or an N.I.H. postdoc at fifty-five thousand dollars.

239
00:26:53,840 --> 00:26:58,400
The student debt does not care about your feelings, so neither does the graduate.

240
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:03,260
Another brain lost to the death machine. Multiply by forty million.

241
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:10,860
Then wonder why nobody cured your mother's cancer. Printing more money for medicine does not work because the Fed prints

242
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:16,980
even more for war, maintaining the same deadly ratio. The hamster wheel spins faster.

243
00:27:17,320 --> 00:27:21,740
You stay in the same place. The only solution: change the ratio.

244
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:25,860
Take from war. Give to life. That's what the one percent treaty does.
